    {
      "card_id": "card_14_isomers_concept",
      "card_slug": "card_14_isomers_concept",
      "type": "chat",
      "concept_id": "isomers_monosaccharides",
      "level": 2,
      "progress": {
        "current": 14,
        "total": 72
      },
      "messages": [
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Dekho Raju, same atoms lekin different arrangement! Jaise 'LISTEN' aur 'SILENT' same letters hain but different words. Chemistry mein isko ISOMERISM kehte hain. Glucose, Fructose, Galactose teeno C₆H₁₂O₆ hain lekin atoms ki arrangement different hai, isliye properties different!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Achhaaaa... matlab structure matter karta hai formula se zyada!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "aman",
          "text": "Exactly! Ab ek important classification aur - carbon atoms ki sankhya ke basis pe:\n🔸 TRIOSE (3 carbons) - rare\n🔸 PENTOSE (5 carbons) - Ribose, Deoxyribose (DNA/RNA mein!)\n🔸 HEXOSE (6 carbons) - Glucose, Fructose, Galactose (most common)\n\nHexoses sabse abundant hain nature mein. SSC mein direct pucha jata hai!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "raju",
          "text": "Sir pentose DNA/RNA mein hota hai? Ye to biology wala topic lag raha hai! 🤔"
